1
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:40,100
[River of No Return]

2
00:01:40,130 --> 00:01:43,020
[Episode 11: Into the Tiger's Den]

3
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:44,710
Go out from here,

4
00:01:45,180 --> 00:01:46,400
pass a hall,

5
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:47,780
and take the covered walkway.

6
00:01:47,780 --> 00:01:49,789
The room on the left is the study.

7
00:01:50,930 --> 00:01:52,530
Is there anyone guarding it?

8
00:01:53,570 --> 00:01:54,120
No.

9
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:54,930
There isn't.

10
00:01:55,470 --> 00:01:56,070
Wait.

11
00:02:02,070 --> 00:02:03,270
The letter of passage

12
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:05,670
needs your master's seal, doesn't it?

13
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:08,620
Speak!

14
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:12,260
The letter of passage

15
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:14,740
won't be valid unless it bears

16
00:02:15,410 --> 00:02:16,530
our master's seal.

17
00:02:22,550 --> 00:02:23,460
Don't move.

18
00:02:33,620 --> 00:02:34,500
Steward Wang.

19
00:02:34,850 --> 00:02:36,310
Send a reliable attendant

20
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:37,720
to go with my friend here.

21
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:40,250
Tell whoever writes the letter of passage

22
00:02:40,250 --> 00:02:41,570
that it's on your orders.

23
00:02:41,570 --> 00:02:42,340
Understood?

24
00:02:44,370 --> 00:02:45,090
Got it.

25
00:02:45,610 --> 00:02:46,170
Okay.

26
00:02:46,470 --> 00:02:47,160
Shisan!

27
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:54,340
Little Xingren is right.

28
00:02:54,780 --> 00:02:56,510
Don't cause any extra trouble.

29
00:03:06,070 --> 00:03:06,610
Move!

30
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:15,620
Behave yourself.

31
00:03:20,370 --> 00:03:21,010
Sir,

32
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:21,880
this way.

33
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:35,060
Sir.

34
00:03:35,470 --> 00:03:36,060
This way.

35
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:43,320
♪ The bamboo clappers clatter away ♪

36
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:45,440
♪ As I, the bookkeeper,
go over the accounts ♪

37
00:03:45,460 --> 00:03:47,440
♪ Salt ships come and go along the canal ♪

38
00:03:47,470 --> 00:03:49,470
♪ Goods from north and south
bring profits home ♪

39
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:51,550
♪ Our master's wealth is beyond compare ♪

40
00:03:51,579 --> 00:03:53,670
♪ Gold and silver fill his mansion
with flair ♪

41
00:03:53,690 --> 00:03:55,750
♪ I record each entry meticulously,
one by one ♪

42
00:03:55,770 --> 00:03:57,670
♪ Not a single coin
can be misplaced there ♪

43
00:03:57,690 --> 00:03:59,680
♪ The sums go on,
the counting won't cease ♪

44
00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:03,000
♪ A ceaseless flow of money,
boundless and endless ♪

45
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:04,370
Who's this?

46
00:04:04,690 --> 00:04:06,060
He's a friend of Wang Da's—

47
00:04:06,060 --> 00:04:06,860
one of our own.

48
00:04:07,570 --> 00:04:09,830
Wang Da promised him a letter of passage.

49
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:14,490
Here's the seal.

50
00:04:18,310 --> 00:04:19,769
When do you plan to set out?

51
00:04:19,810 --> 00:04:20,390
Today.

52
00:04:21,390 --> 00:04:23,360
I'm afraid you won't make it today.

53
00:04:23,750 --> 00:04:25,950
The earliest would be tomorrow at dawn.

54
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:29,690
Lean back.

55
00:04:31,100 --> 00:04:31,980
Young Master.

56
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:34,570
You've got the letter of passage you want.

57
00:04:34,650 --> 00:04:35,800
Can you let us go now?

58
00:04:44,130 --> 00:04:45,620
I was just momentarily

59
00:04:45,870 --> 00:04:46,980
blinded by greed.

60
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:50,060
Momentarily blinded?

61
00:04:58,750 --> 00:04:59,659
To be honest,

62
00:05:00,370 --> 00:05:02,240
ever since the incident in Jinling,

63
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:05,830
a letter of passage from our Wang family
has been worth a fortune.

64
00:05:05,830 --> 00:05:06,740
If our master finds out about this...

65
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:08,400
You think this is about money?

66
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:12,360
The canal stretches for thousands of li,

67
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:15,010
yet a mere merchant family like yours

68
00:05:15,010 --> 00:05:18,250
has managed to seize the power
to grant or withhold favors at will.

69
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:21,100
That's all thanks to our master's
careful management.

70
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:22,330
And as you said yourself,

71
00:05:22,330 --> 00:05:23,790
this canal stretches for thousands of li—

72
00:05:23,790 --> 00:05:26,990
which official hasn't enjoyed
the Wang family's favors?

73
00:05:28,940 --> 00:05:30,620
No wonder everyone says

74
00:05:31,770 --> 00:05:33,210
that scum Wang Ji

75
00:05:34,090 --> 00:05:35,860
truly is living in luxury.

76
00:05:36,740 --> 00:05:37,800
But the Wang family

77
00:05:38,370 --> 00:05:40,310
supports half the people in Yangzhou.

78
00:05:40,310 --> 00:05:41,980
Isn't that also helping ease
the imperial court's burdens?

79
00:05:41,980 --> 00:05:42,909
What did you say?

80
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:43,810
Let him speak.

81
00:05:44,659 --> 00:05:45,590
Didn't the court

82
00:05:45,690 --> 00:05:47,040
introduce the transshipment system

83
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:49,450
just to bring profits
under government control?

84
00:05:49,450 --> 00:05:51,270
And where do the government's profits
come from?

85
00:05:51,270 --> 00:05:53,530
Don't they have to rely on people like us?

86
00:05:56,130 --> 00:05:58,090
That's utter nonsense.

87
00:05:59,510 --> 00:06:01,240
The transshipment system
was clearly designed

88
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:02,770
to ease the people's burden

89
00:06:02,860 --> 00:06:04,860
and improve transport efficiency.

90
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:08,660
Since when was it about bringing profits
under government control?

91
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:09,790
Even the best policy

92
00:06:10,450 --> 00:06:13,190
needs to offer people an incentive
if you want it implemented,

93
00:06:13,190 --> 00:06:13,740
right?

94
00:06:13,950 --> 00:06:16,210
His Majesty sits deep within the palace,

95
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:19,520
so it's only natural that he doesn't
understand the realities on the ground.

96
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:21,380
Everything has its pros and cons.

97
00:06:21,810 --> 00:06:23,950
First he wants to move the capital,
then he wants to abolish grain transport—

98
00:06:23,950 --> 00:06:26,360
and in the end,
he even sacrifices his own son.

99
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:27,690
That's hardly worth it,

100
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:28,500
is it?

101
00:06:34,180 --> 00:06:36,240
So you all want the Crown Prince dead?

102
00:06:39,620 --> 00:06:41,980
The one who truly wants
the Crown Prince dead

103
00:06:41,980 --> 00:06:42,909
is someone else.

104
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:44,980
Our master

105
00:06:45,570 --> 00:06:47,630
is the last person who wants him dead.

106
00:06:48,130 --> 00:06:50,480
Then why did he send a treasure ship
full of explosives?

107
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:51,500
It was a frame-up!

108
00:06:51,590 --> 00:06:53,850
Someone was trying to pin the blame on us!

109
00:06:55,450 --> 00:06:56,780
Still putting on an act?

110
00:07:08,540 --> 00:07:09,140
Thank you.

111
00:07:15,370 --> 00:07:16,540
Let's go. Let's go.

112
00:07:16,660 --> 00:07:17,660
Come on, let's go.

113
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:28,000
I, Wang Ji, respectfully welcome you,

114
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:32,059
Eunuch Zhu, Superintendent of
the Directorate of the Imperial Stables.

115
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:41,210
Which way?

116
00:08:50,300 --> 00:08:52,450
Eunuch Zhu, your personal visit
to my humble home

117
00:08:52,450 --> 00:08:54,450
must mean you have something important
to tell me.

118
00:08:54,450 --> 00:08:55,610
I'm all ears...

119
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:57,340
My surname isn't Zhu.

120
00:08:57,810 --> 00:08:59,740
The man you call Eunuch Zhu is dead.

121
00:09:00,380 --> 00:09:02,140
The man I want to kill is actually
surnamed Zhu.

122
00:09:02,140 --> 00:09:04,770
[Wang Ji, Yangzhou Merchant]

123
00:09:10,970 --> 00:09:11,710
Tell me,

124
00:09:12,020 --> 00:09:14,080
what's the thing I've seen most often

125
00:09:14,540 --> 00:09:15,810
in my life?

126
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:19,260
You've seen all manner of things.

127
00:09:19,280 --> 00:09:20,810
How could I possibly guess?

128
00:09:21,110 --> 00:09:22,440
People's expressions.

129
00:09:22,970 --> 00:09:24,430
All kinds of expressions.

130
00:09:25,730 --> 00:09:26,330
I'll pass.

131
00:09:26,590 --> 00:09:27,490
Please, help yourself.

132
00:09:27,490 --> 00:09:28,420
Now, tell me,

133
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:30,230
what's the thing

134
00:09:31,330 --> 00:09:33,060
I've said most often in my life?

135
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:33,780
Praise.

136
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:34,900
Flattery.

137
00:09:35,310 --> 00:09:36,680
All sorts of auspicious words.

138
00:09:36,680 --> 00:09:37,730
Lies.

139
00:09:39,420 --> 00:09:40,420
I'm no different.

140
00:09:40,730 --> 00:09:41,490
I'm no different.

141
00:09:41,490 --> 00:09:42,550
You're different.

142
00:09:43,710 --> 00:09:45,040
You still have a chance.

143
00:09:46,180 --> 00:09:47,230
I do have a chance—

144
00:09:47,830 --> 00:09:50,030
a chance to die in someone else's place.

145
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:51,060
You mustn't die.

146
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:52,450
You've got to win.

147
00:09:52,940 --> 00:09:54,200
Only by winning can you

148
00:09:54,710 --> 00:09:58,190
preserve the legacy your Wang family
has built over generations.

149
00:09:58,190 --> 00:10:00,090
You're quite the liar yourself,
Eunuch Zhu.

150
00:10:00,090 --> 00:10:01,570
If I'm dead,

151
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:03,780
how am I supposed to
care about any of that?

152
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:06,640
You don't really believe
what the books say, do you?

153
00:10:08,490 --> 00:10:09,140
All right,

154
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:10,140
enough beating around the bush.

155
00:10:10,140 --> 00:10:11,670
Let's get down to business.

156
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:15,360
Have there been any cormorants
with their necks tied up

157
00:10:15,420 --> 00:10:18,750
heading to Beijing via your route
these past couple of days?

158
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:20,800
To tell you the truth,

159
00:10:21,570 --> 00:10:23,570
there are some at the dock every day.

160
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:28,260
I'm looking for

161
00:10:29,810 --> 00:10:30,570
4 people.

162
00:10:31,570 --> 00:10:32,900
Three men and one woman.

163
00:10:33,850 --> 00:10:35,780
They're willing to pay a hefty sum.

164
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:39,300
I heard there might be two men,

165
00:10:39,950 --> 00:10:42,610
one scholarly-looking
and the other a fighter.

166
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:44,330
Can you get the ship owner here?

167
00:10:44,330 --> 00:10:44,990
Certainly.

168
00:10:45,690 --> 00:10:47,780
I'll send someone to fetch them
right away.

169
00:10:47,780 --> 00:10:48,310
Alright.

170
00:10:48,850 --> 00:10:49,780
Enjoy your food.

171
00:11:02,190 --> 00:11:02,990
Young Master.

172
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:09,930
Turn your face away.

173
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:10,810
Turn away!

174
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:21,940
Can I have a word with you?

175
00:11:30,110 --> 00:11:30,910
Young Master.

176
00:11:32,060 --> 00:11:33,920
Good-for-Nothing has been gone
for quite some time.

177
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:36,260
Could he have run off
with the letter of passage?

178
00:11:36,260 --> 00:11:38,260
Perhaps we should pull back for now.

179
00:11:40,020 --> 00:11:41,350
Let's wait a bit longer.

180
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:43,380
Young Master.

181
00:11:43,940 --> 00:11:44,920
Back when we were in Jinling,

182
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:48,120
Good-for-Nothing kept asking me for money
at every turn.

183
00:11:48,190 --> 00:11:50,020
That letter of passage is worth
far more than

184
00:11:50,020 --> 00:11:51,550
the 2,000 taels we paid him.

185
00:11:54,030 --> 00:11:55,990
A good minister may be foolish but loyal,
while a loyal minister may be slow-witted.

186
00:11:55,990 --> 00:11:58,180
Extraordinary times
call for extraordinary men.

187
00:11:58,180 --> 00:12:00,300
He may seem like a carefree rogue,

188
00:12:00,570 --> 00:12:02,500
but he has yet to go back on his word.

189
00:12:02,540 --> 00:12:04,270
Since things have come to this,

190
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:06,000
let's take it one step a time.

191
00:12:07,520 --> 00:12:08,200
But, Your Highness...

192
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:09,540
Across the 2 capitals and 13 provinces

193
00:12:09,540 --> 00:12:11,950
of our Ming Empire, there are
hundreds, even thousands of officials.

194
00:12:11,950 --> 00:12:13,750
If not one of them can be trusted,

195
00:12:13,760 --> 00:12:15,890
then not one of them can be relied upon.

196
00:12:17,330 --> 00:12:18,730
Let's give him more time.

197
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:28,580
Since we've chosen to stand together
through thick and thin,

198
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:32,960
we shouldn't keep suspecting one another.

199
00:12:37,730 --> 00:12:38,420
This way.

200
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:40,810
Come on, this way.

201
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:49,160
This way, please.

202
00:12:56,070 --> 00:12:56,810
Master Wang.

203
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:58,890
[Xie Sanfa, Ship Owner]

204
00:12:58,310 --> 00:13:00,470
You can't bully us just because
you're in a position of power.

205
00:13:00,470 --> 00:13:01,830
We're just small-time merchants,

206
00:13:01,830 --> 00:13:04,060
and we haven't owed a single coin in fees.

207
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:06,210
You can't just seize our ship like that.

208
00:13:06,210 --> 00:13:08,610
Who said anything about seizing your ship?

209
00:13:09,710 --> 00:13:11,770
Someone wants to see the three of you.

210
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:23,830
So you are Xie Sanfa?

211
00:13:24,190 --> 00:13:24,780
Yes.

212
00:13:25,330 --> 00:13:26,190
The ship owner?

213
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:27,080
That's right.

214
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:29,040
Where did your ship come from?

215
00:13:33,180 --> 00:13:33,780
Zhoushan.

216
00:13:33,990 --> 00:13:36,390
Do you guys have
wives and children at home?

217
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:37,970
My Lord, what exactly

218
00:13:37,970 --> 00:13:38,710
are you trying to find out?

219
00:13:38,710 --> 00:13:40,640
Why all the roundabout questions?

220
00:13:40,900 --> 00:13:41,960
Watch your tongue.

221
00:13:42,660 --> 00:13:45,990
All three of them come from
families of boatmen in Zhoushan.

222
00:13:47,920 --> 00:13:50,320
So how much profit do you make
on a shipment?

223
00:13:50,710 --> 00:13:52,610
Depends on the destination.

224
00:13:53,180 --> 00:13:54,310
What about Beijing?

225
00:13:55,730 --> 00:13:57,940
With favorable winds and smooth sailing,

226
00:13:57,940 --> 00:13:58,570
about 20%.

227
00:14:03,330 --> 00:14:05,060
I think these three will do.

228
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:06,980
Sanfa, what's this about?

229
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:08,330
You...

230
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:15,900
Don't be afraid.

231
00:14:16,950 --> 00:14:18,480
As long as you make sure
the four cormorants

232
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:20,950
you're supposed to pick up get on board,

233
00:14:22,180 --> 00:14:24,060
all this money is yours.

234
00:14:26,010 --> 00:14:26,630
Master.

235
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:30,220
We're boatmen, not hired muscle.

236
00:14:31,810 --> 00:14:32,880
We don't risk our lives for money.

237
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:34,340
There's no avoiding that.

238
00:14:36,830 --> 00:14:37,760
Name your price.

239
00:15:06,670 --> 00:15:07,600
Don't look back!

240
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:10,660
Did you get the letter of passage?

241
00:15:12,590 --> 00:15:13,420
I did.

242
00:15:14,160 --> 00:15:14,900
Who are you?

243
00:15:15,180 --> 00:15:16,440
Why are you helping me?

244
00:15:37,740 --> 00:15:39,550
Wang Ji had no idea that Huliu explosive

245
00:15:39,550 --> 00:15:41,190
had been secretly stashed aboard
the treasure ship?

246
00:15:41,190 --> 00:15:42,400
He truly didn't know.

247
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:45,020
And he has even less idea

248
00:15:45,850 --> 00:15:48,450
who was pulling the strings
behind the scenes?

249
00:15:48,780 --> 00:15:50,090
That's correct.

250
00:15:56,490 --> 00:15:58,620
So you know absolutely nothing at all.

251
00:15:58,760 --> 00:15:59,830
Then why did you try to capture us

252
00:15:59,830 --> 00:16:01,260
the moment we walked in?

253
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:05,680
The people at the gambling den said

254
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:09,440
your young master had an unusually skilled
way of fighting crickets,

255
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:11,440
and they assumed you were from the palace.

256
00:16:11,440 --> 00:16:12,570
We only detained you

257
00:16:12,730 --> 00:16:14,090
to get a chance

258
00:16:14,330 --> 00:16:15,660
to tell the truth.

259
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:17,900
Well done.

260
00:16:19,970 --> 00:16:21,940
Truly well done.

261
00:16:24,090 --> 00:16:26,180
Even with death staring you in the face,

262
00:16:26,180 --> 00:16:29,040
you're still finding ways
to cover for your master.

263
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:31,970
We'll see who's really facing death here.

264
00:16:49,810 --> 00:16:50,610
Did you get it?

265
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:51,490
I did.

266
00:16:53,210 --> 00:16:54,110
We can't stay here any longer.

267
00:16:54,110 --> 00:16:55,040
Let's get going.

268
00:16:55,800 --> 00:16:57,000
What about these men?

269
00:16:57,260 --> 00:16:59,190
They've seen Young Master's face.

270
00:16:59,350 --> 00:17:00,680
We have to silence them.

271
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:01,340
Don't move!

272
00:17:01,470 --> 00:17:02,330
Nobody move!

273
00:17:05,619 --> 00:17:07,280
Plenty of people have seen us.

274
00:17:07,599 --> 00:17:08,700
Are we supposed to kill them all?

275
00:17:08,700 --> 00:17:10,069
Word could get out.

276
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:11,420
If this leads to trouble,

277
00:17:11,420 --> 00:17:12,470
we could lose sight of the bigger picture
over a small matter!

278
00:17:12,470 --> 00:17:13,280
Enough talk.

279
00:17:14,530 --> 00:17:16,990
You're a constable.
Find a way to handle this.

280
00:17:16,990 --> 00:17:17,839
Take him away.

281
00:17:18,099 --> 00:17:18,640
Let's go!

282
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:24,859
Get up!

283
00:17:32,330 --> 00:17:33,750
If you want to live,

284
00:17:34,010 --> 00:17:35,100
behave yourselves

285
00:17:35,450 --> 00:17:36,710
and don't go anywhere.

286
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:40,260
♪ Along the Qinhuai River in Nanjing ♪

287
00:17:40,300 --> 00:17:42,230
♪ I patrol the streets,
swaying along day after day ♪

288
00:17:42,260 --> 00:17:43,690
♪ A jug of wine in hand,
a blade of grass between my teeth ♪

289
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:45,210
♪ Even the rowdiest ghosts run
when they see me ♪

290
00:17:45,230 --> 00:17:47,100
♪ Through storms and flames, I press on ♪

291
00:17:47,120 --> 00:17:48,780
♪ I drag my life along like a rope ♪

292
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:50,400
♪ They call me a young constable ♪

293
00:17:50,430 --> 00:17:52,120
♪ But this realm isn't mine to rule ♪

294
00:17:52,140 --> 00:17:54,710
♪ Isn't mine to rule ♪

295
00:17:58,790 --> 00:17:59,580
What are you doing?

296
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:00,140
Come out.

297
00:18:00,860 --> 00:18:01,530
I... I...

298
00:18:04,300 --> 00:18:05,230
Little Xingren.

299
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:10,770
You must not let him know

300
00:18:10,970 --> 00:18:12,030
where we are going.

301
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:16,730
Take this iron ruler

302
00:18:16,870 --> 00:18:17,400
with you.

303
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:23,820
Blindfold him

304
00:18:24,660 --> 00:18:26,660
and take him as far away as possible.

305
00:18:35,290 --> 00:18:35,860
Get up.

306
00:18:36,530 --> 00:18:37,490
Get up!

307
00:18:40,080 --> 00:18:40,880
Go over there.

308
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:43,160
Stop looking!

309
00:18:44,690 --> 00:18:45,490
Rectifier Yu.

310
00:18:47,030 --> 00:18:47,730
Don't look.

311
00:18:51,340 --> 00:18:52,140
Young Master.

312
00:18:52,990 --> 00:18:54,160
Don't take his life.

313
00:18:56,050 --> 00:18:57,530
As if I could.

314
00:19:00,620 --> 00:19:01,180
Here.

315
00:19:06,010 --> 00:19:06,530
Move.

316
00:19:07,290 --> 00:19:07,900
Move!

317
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:19,340
You sent him away on purpose, didn't you?

318
00:19:22,270 --> 00:19:23,330
There's something

319
00:19:23,420 --> 00:19:24,550
I must tell you.

320
00:19:27,230 --> 00:19:28,030
Zhu Bukha

321
00:19:28,630 --> 00:19:29,490
is still alive.

322
00:19:34,820 --> 00:19:37,660
We both saw him fall into the water
with our own eyes.

323
00:19:37,660 --> 00:19:39,390
Where did you see him this time?

324
00:19:39,660 --> 00:19:40,990
At Wang Ji's residence.

325
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:42,520
I saw him with my own eyes.

326
00:19:42,600 --> 00:19:43,580
I witnessed him

327
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:45,600
bribing that ship owner, Xie Sanfa.

328
00:19:49,970 --> 00:19:51,800
Zhu Bukha really is hard to kill.

329
00:19:53,090 --> 00:19:54,420
I also found Huliu explosive

330
00:19:54,420 --> 00:19:56,550
in the woodshed at the Wang residence.

331
00:19:56,600 --> 00:19:57,210
Wang Ji

332
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:58,680
cannot escape the blame.

333
00:20:01,320 --> 00:20:02,100
Now that

334
00:20:02,660 --> 00:20:04,390
we've got the letter of passage

335
00:20:04,680 --> 00:20:05,580
and a ship,

336
00:20:08,100 --> 00:20:10,030
should we make our escape tonight?

337
00:20:10,990 --> 00:20:11,620
Escape?

338
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:14,850
I fled from Dongshuiguan Wharf

339
00:20:15,180 --> 00:20:16,580
to the palace in Jinling,

340
00:20:16,870 --> 00:20:19,330
then from the palace in Jinling
to Yangzhou.

341
00:20:19,730 --> 00:20:21,420
If we keep running like this,

342
00:20:21,600 --> 00:20:23,530
I'll never make it back to Beijing.

343
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:26,360
I don't want to run either.

344
00:20:28,510 --> 00:20:29,580
My father's death

345
00:20:30,450 --> 00:20:32,430
has everything to do with Zhu Bukha.

346
00:20:32,430 --> 00:20:34,540
I want him dead more than anything.

347
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:37,560
But if we go head-to-head
with Zhu Bukha now,

348
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:39,900
will you ever make it back to Beijing?

349
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:44,010
Don't forget,

350
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:46,250
he's after me.

351
00:20:47,070 --> 00:20:48,590
If I'm on the ship,

352
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:50,930
he'll definitely come aboard.

353
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:54,460
You're going to use yourself as bait?

354
00:20:56,340 --> 00:20:58,000
We don't have much choice now.

355
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:02,580
I'm willing to take my chances

356
00:21:03,210 --> 00:21:04,620
with Little Xingren.

357
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:06,660
But you're different.

358
00:21:08,250 --> 00:21:09,580
What's the difference?

359
00:21:10,380 --> 00:21:12,380
We've all had to fight for our lives.

360
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:14,000
Every life is worth the same.

361
00:21:15,450 --> 00:21:17,050
If disaster is unavoidable,

362
00:21:17,450 --> 00:21:19,310
then let's settle things with him

363
00:21:19,540 --> 00:21:20,890
right here and now.

364
00:21:26,250 --> 00:21:27,050
Officer,

365
00:21:27,990 --> 00:21:29,520
which yamen do you serve in?

366
00:21:32,010 --> 00:21:34,070
What makes you think I'm an official?

367
00:21:36,290 --> 00:21:36,770
Move!

368
00:21:38,970 --> 00:21:39,820
To be honest,

369
00:21:40,680 --> 00:21:42,880
I used to serve in the Ministry of Rites.

370
00:21:45,530 --> 00:21:47,390
You're different from those two.

371
00:21:47,490 --> 00:21:49,280
The way you speak and conduct yourself

372
00:21:49,280 --> 00:21:51,410
shows you know some proper etiquette.

373
00:21:53,820 --> 00:21:55,220
What else did you notice?

374
00:21:55,900 --> 00:21:56,700
Keep talking!

375
00:21:57,400 --> 00:21:58,530
If I'm not mistaken,

376
00:21:59,450 --> 00:22:00,180
that one

377
00:22:00,600 --> 00:22:02,260
is the Crown Prince, isn't he?

378
00:22:05,670 --> 00:22:06,330
Well,

379
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:09,720
looks like I really

380
00:22:10,550 --> 00:22:12,010
can't let you leave today.

381
00:22:12,360 --> 00:22:13,190
What do you want?

382
00:22:13,190 --> 00:22:14,560
I want to kill you!

383
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:17,910
I dare you look again.

384
00:22:19,010 --> 00:22:19,660
I dare you!

385
00:22:26,610 --> 00:22:27,900
If you want me dead, do it then.

386
00:22:27,900 --> 00:22:28,560
Don't move!

387
00:22:30,830 --> 00:22:31,410
Come on.

388
00:22:53,840 --> 00:22:55,560
Being so indecisive,

389
00:22:57,080 --> 00:22:59,010
let alone enjoy being an official,

390
00:22:59,610 --> 00:23:01,740
life itself must be no fun to you at all.

391
00:23:04,660 --> 00:23:06,660
I know you look down on us merchants.

392
00:23:06,950 --> 00:23:09,680
You despise us for
putting profit above loyalty.

393
00:23:09,710 --> 00:23:11,210
But how noble

394
00:23:11,470 --> 00:23:13,180
are your own motives?

395
00:23:14,470 --> 00:23:16,190
Aren't you escorting the Crown Prince

396
00:23:16,190 --> 00:23:17,940
to secure a promotion

397
00:23:18,080 --> 00:23:19,340
and greater fortune?

398
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:21,380
Are you done?

399
00:23:29,820 --> 00:23:31,250
I'll give you two words:

400
00:23:31,660 --> 00:23:32,730
utter nonsense.

401
00:23:40,840 --> 00:23:42,170
My great-grandfather,

402
00:23:42,250 --> 00:23:45,620
great-great-grandfather, and grandfather
all served as officials.

403
00:23:45,620 --> 00:23:47,470
Each served the people in his post,

404
00:23:47,470 --> 00:23:49,120
never seeking wealth or glory,

405
00:23:49,120 --> 00:23:50,850
never shying away from danger.

406
00:23:54,030 --> 00:23:55,660
My guiding principle is:

407
00:23:57,120 --> 00:23:59,530
"When poor, cultivate oneself;

408
00:24:00,760 --> 00:24:03,910
when prosperous, benefit the world."

409
00:24:05,450 --> 00:24:07,250
I would rather sacrifice my life

410
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:10,600
than compromise my principles.

411
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:19,020
Compared to a shallow, fickle man

412
00:24:20,550 --> 00:24:22,280
like you, who resigned his post

413
00:24:23,710 --> 00:24:25,170
to chase wealth and grovel

414
00:24:25,580 --> 00:24:27,110
before the stench of money,

415
00:24:29,990 --> 00:24:31,530
we're worlds apart.

416
00:24:36,190 --> 00:24:37,250
Today, right here,

417
00:24:38,890 --> 00:24:40,300
mark my words:

418
00:24:43,920 --> 00:24:47,850
I'm the Right Rectifier of the
Right Secretariat of the Heir Apparent,

419
00:24:49,430 --> 00:24:50,630
and my name is Yu Qian.

420
00:24:55,250 --> 00:24:57,940
Don't make yourself out to be
so noble and righteous.

421
00:24:57,940 --> 00:24:59,740
Those grand, high-minded words

422
00:24:59,750 --> 00:25:00,900
might fool others,

423
00:25:01,080 --> 00:25:02,740
but they won't fool yourself.

424
00:25:03,050 --> 00:25:04,530
You're escorting the Crown Prince
to the capital

425
00:25:04,530 --> 00:25:06,730
for the sake of a promotion and fortune!

426
00:25:06,730 --> 00:25:08,530
We merchants, on the other hand,

427
00:25:08,530 --> 00:25:10,730
are just trying to put food on the table!

428
00:25:10,860 --> 00:25:12,260
It's just that I'm tired.

429
00:25:12,660 --> 00:25:13,770
I'm so tired.

430
00:25:14,440 --> 00:25:15,530
And I know

431
00:25:16,140 --> 00:25:17,800
I'm no longer of any use to you.

432
00:25:18,680 --> 00:25:19,480
Make it quick.

433
00:25:20,140 --> 00:25:21,450
Don't make me suffer.

434
00:25:22,780 --> 00:25:23,980
Just get it over with.

435
00:25:43,360 --> 00:25:44,620
Where's His Highness?

436
00:25:44,930 --> 00:25:46,990
Where did you leave that Wang fellow?

437
00:25:46,990 --> 00:25:47,860
Tied him up on the ship.

438
00:25:47,860 --> 00:25:48,590
Don't worry.

439
00:25:50,270 --> 00:25:51,340
Are you an idiot?

440
00:25:51,670 --> 00:25:53,800
Whose territory do you think we're in?

441
00:25:57,060 --> 00:25:58,470
Within 4 hours,

442
00:25:59,120 --> 00:26:00,750
I'm sure someone from the Wang family

443
00:26:00,750 --> 00:26:02,150
will come and rescue him.

444
00:26:04,730 --> 00:26:06,100
Then what was I supposed to do?

445
00:26:06,100 --> 00:26:07,230
Kill him, of course.

446
00:26:09,320 --> 00:26:10,320
Come on, you do it.

447
00:26:10,630 --> 00:26:11,490
You go kill him.

448
00:26:13,970 --> 00:26:15,220
Just walk 500 steps that way.

449
00:26:15,220 --> 00:26:16,820
Alright, you hurry up and go.

450
00:26:16,970 --> 00:26:17,770
Stop arguing.

451
00:26:18,100 --> 00:26:20,300
We just need to be one step ahead of them.

452
00:26:22,030 --> 00:26:25,090
-Couldn't even handle that.
-You only know how to talk.

453
00:26:32,010 --> 00:26:32,770
Come out.

454
00:26:34,400 --> 00:26:36,200
I know you've been following me.

455
00:26:45,470 --> 00:26:46,820
You saved my life.

456
00:26:48,230 --> 00:26:49,530
If you don't come out,

457
00:26:50,290 --> 00:26:51,950
how am I supposed to thank you?

458
00:27:11,050 --> 00:27:12,050
You hit me so hard.

459
00:27:17,750 --> 00:27:19,480
Are you from the Iron Alliance?

460
00:27:19,590 --> 00:27:22,000
[Zuo Yehe, Envoy of the Iron Alliance]

461
00:27:19,710 --> 00:27:21,310
Where did you hide my sister?

462
00:27:21,710 --> 00:27:22,470
Release her already.

463
00:27:22,470 --> 00:27:23,400
She's innocent.

464
00:27:23,530 --> 00:27:24,660
Your sister is safe.

465
00:27:25,120 --> 00:27:25,820
Besides,

466
00:27:26,320 --> 00:27:28,120
didn't I save you during the day?

467
00:27:28,250 --> 00:27:29,580
Don't I deserve a thank-you from you?

468
00:27:29,580 --> 00:27:30,980
Of course you deserve it.

469
00:27:31,230 --> 00:27:32,140
But first, you have to tell me

470
00:27:32,140 --> 00:27:33,250
why you saved me.

471
00:27:34,420 --> 00:27:36,950
Because you're the one
I've been looking for.

472
00:27:37,810 --> 00:27:38,400
Me?

473
00:27:41,030 --> 00:27:43,160
Wait, why have you been looking for me?

474
00:27:44,840 --> 00:27:45,500
To help you.

475
00:27:46,900 --> 00:27:48,450
So you helped me,

476
00:27:49,380 --> 00:27:50,340
and you expect me

477
00:27:50,360 --> 00:27:51,650
to thank you for it?

478
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:56,050
Come with me

479
00:27:56,880 --> 00:27:57,740
to see someone.

480
00:27:58,530 --> 00:28:00,420
Hey, why should I trust you?

481
00:28:04,940 --> 00:28:06,940
You'll need my help sooner or later.

482
00:28:09,640 --> 00:28:11,570
Why not start by working together?

483
00:28:19,490 --> 00:28:20,180
All right.

484
00:28:21,250 --> 00:28:22,580
I do have one thing

485
00:28:22,840 --> 00:28:23,580
to ask of you.

486
00:28:55,250 --> 00:28:56,050
Steward Wang?

487
00:29:00,380 --> 00:29:02,710
Have you dealt with those troublemakers?

488
00:29:05,920 --> 00:29:06,730
Are you okay?

489
00:29:07,100 --> 00:29:07,710
Master.

490
00:29:08,330 --> 00:29:10,570
I... I almost didn't make it back.

491
00:29:13,230 --> 00:29:14,530
Who are those three?

492
00:29:14,880 --> 00:29:16,100
If I'm not mistaken,

493
00:29:16,600 --> 00:29:17,660
one of them

494
00:29:18,270 --> 00:29:19,440
is the Crown Prince.

495
00:29:25,820 --> 00:29:26,820
That explains it.

496
00:29:28,690 --> 00:29:31,490
Eunuch Zhu from Jinling
has also come to Yangzhou.

497
00:29:32,320 --> 00:29:32,970
Master.

498
00:29:33,640 --> 00:29:35,550
If the Crown Prince has really
come to Yangzhou,

499
00:29:35,550 --> 00:29:37,550
will that spell fortune or disaster

500
00:29:37,690 --> 00:29:39,180
for our Wang family?

501
00:29:54,840 --> 00:29:56,450
Either way,

502
00:29:56,780 --> 00:29:58,240
it's no good for us.

503
00:29:59,470 --> 00:30:00,690
After the treasure ship explosion,

504
00:30:00,690 --> 00:30:03,090
the Crown Prince will never
trust me again.

505
00:30:04,010 --> 00:30:05,270
But if we help Zhu Bukha

506
00:30:05,840 --> 00:30:07,190
and the Crown Prince manages to escape,

507
00:30:07,190 --> 00:30:07,960
our Wang family

508
00:30:07,960 --> 00:30:09,570
will definitely be doomed.

509
00:30:10,970 --> 00:30:11,490
But...

510
00:30:12,480 --> 00:30:14,880
But we can't just sit around
and do nothing.

511
00:30:21,290 --> 00:30:22,490
Helping neither side

512
00:30:24,340 --> 00:30:25,820
means owing neither side.

513
00:30:26,790 --> 00:30:27,730
Let them

514
00:30:28,710 --> 00:30:30,820
fight it out and see who comes out on top.

515
00:30:30,820 --> 00:30:32,750
Then we'll simply go with the flow.

516
00:30:35,950 --> 00:30:37,080
For now, all we can do

517
00:30:37,790 --> 00:30:39,100
is wait.

518
00:30:52,160 --> 00:30:54,580
[Guazhou Ferry]

519
00:31:24,690 --> 00:31:25,490
Young Master.

520
00:31:26,230 --> 00:31:28,160
We can leave Yangzhou first thing
tomorrow morning

521
00:31:28,160 --> 00:31:29,020
and head north.

522
00:31:29,900 --> 00:31:31,640
We'll first pass through Huai'an,

523
00:31:31,640 --> 00:31:33,940
then rest briefly by the ancient canal.

524
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:37,600
From there, we'll continue to Xuzhou
and change boats.

525
00:31:37,600 --> 00:31:39,400
Then we can make haste all the way

526
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:41,490
to Tianjin,

527
00:31:41,920 --> 00:31:43,580
where we'll switch to horses.

528
00:31:44,180 --> 00:31:46,120
After that, you can
ride straight into Beijing

529
00:31:46,120 --> 00:31:47,320
to put down the rebels

530
00:31:48,130 --> 00:31:49,490
and inherit the throne.

531
00:31:58,510 --> 00:31:59,420
Rectifier Yu.

532
00:31:59,940 --> 00:32:01,070
Yes, Your Highness.

533
00:32:01,270 --> 00:32:02,250
Back in Jinling,

534
00:32:04,140 --> 00:32:05,540
I already suspected that

535
00:32:05,970 --> 00:32:07,770
whether it was the Iron Alliance

536
00:32:08,160 --> 00:32:09,250
or Wang Ji,

537
00:32:09,940 --> 00:32:12,200
anyone daring to murder the Crown Prince

538
00:32:15,360 --> 00:32:16,340
must be backed by

539
00:32:18,660 --> 00:32:20,290
someone from the Zhu family.

540
00:32:22,640 --> 00:32:23,640
Your Highness...

541
00:32:26,210 --> 00:32:27,670
I may have no sons of my own,

542
00:32:28,710 --> 00:32:29,420
but I

543
00:32:31,100 --> 00:32:32,760
have 8 fine younger brothers.

544
00:32:42,010 --> 00:32:44,320
Among them, Prince of Xiang
and Prince of Yue

545
00:32:44,320 --> 00:32:46,230
are my full brothers,
born of the same mother.

546
00:32:46,230 --> 00:32:49,230
Your Highness, you mustn't entertain
such thoughts.

547
00:32:49,690 --> 00:32:52,140
That's how things have always been
in the imperial family.

548
00:32:52,140 --> 00:32:54,290
The Crown Prince of Emperor Hongwu

549
00:32:56,050 --> 00:32:57,250
died young.

550
00:33:00,010 --> 00:33:02,070
The Crown Prince of Emperor Jianwen,

551
00:33:02,380 --> 00:33:04,510
Zhu Wenkui, vanished without a trace.

552
00:33:05,070 --> 00:33:07,370
And when Father was the Crown Prince,

553
00:33:08,660 --> 00:33:10,770
he lived every day on tenterhooks.

554
00:33:12,440 --> 00:33:13,050
Why

555
00:33:16,690 --> 00:33:17,450
should I think

556
00:33:17,450 --> 00:33:18,770
I'll be any different?

557
00:33:20,620 --> 00:33:21,900
Whether it's Father

558
00:33:22,290 --> 00:33:23,450
or my uncles,

559
00:33:24,510 --> 00:33:26,240
aren't they all family as well?

560
00:33:27,970 --> 00:33:30,170
I've got nothing to say, Your Highness.

561
00:33:41,250 --> 00:33:42,820
Do you know my second uncle?

562
00:33:43,380 --> 00:33:44,940
Prince of Han, Zhu Gaoxu.

563
00:33:52,910 --> 00:33:54,440
His greatest talent

564
00:33:58,780 --> 00:34:00,520
is fathering sons—

565
00:34:03,450 --> 00:34:05,510
and they're all waiting in the wings.

566
00:35:10,550 --> 00:35:11,420
Dr. Su.

567
00:35:12,900 --> 00:35:16,030
Are you really that eager
to leave with the Crown Prince?

568
00:35:20,260 --> 00:35:21,590
What are you getting at?

569
00:35:22,090 --> 00:35:23,690
Just say what's on your mind.

570
00:35:26,240 --> 00:35:27,220
Are you

571
00:35:27,970 --> 00:35:29,860
hiding something from us?

572
00:35:31,030 --> 00:35:33,160
I'm not sure what you're referring to.

573
00:35:36,920 --> 00:35:38,380
Just how much

574
00:35:38,940 --> 00:35:40,270
are you keeping from us?

575
00:35:44,170 --> 00:35:45,940
We're merely strangers who crossed paths

576
00:35:45,940 --> 00:35:47,800
and happened to travel together.

577
00:35:47,900 --> 00:35:50,030
Once we reach Beijing,
we'll go our separate ways.

578
00:35:50,030 --> 00:35:53,290
So there's no question of
hiding anything from each other.

579
00:35:56,610 --> 00:35:57,380
Dr. Su.

580
00:35:57,800 --> 00:35:58,570
You're back.

581
00:35:59,010 --> 00:36:00,570
We're leaving Yangzhou tomorrow.

582
00:36:00,570 --> 00:36:01,820
Please check

583
00:36:02,070 --> 00:36:03,400
His Highness's arrow wound again.

584
00:36:03,400 --> 00:36:04,650
We can't afford any more mishaps

585
00:36:04,650 --> 00:36:05,650
before we board the ship.

586
00:36:05,650 --> 00:36:06,170
Okay.

587
00:36:06,380 --> 00:36:07,090
Thank you for your trouble.

588
00:36:07,090 --> 00:36:07,750
No problem.

589
00:36:09,360 --> 00:36:10,420
Thank you, Lord Yu.

590
00:36:10,880 --> 00:36:12,610
You certainly are considerate.

591
00:36:12,610 --> 00:36:13,700
That young lady

592
00:36:15,050 --> 00:36:16,380
really knows her stuff.

593
00:36:19,760 --> 00:36:24,300
[Countdown: 12 days]

594
00:36:43,130 --> 00:36:44,570
Send men to scout the surrounding area.

595
00:36:44,570 --> 00:36:45,170
Zhu Zhanji

596
00:36:45,190 --> 00:36:47,120
won't dare show his face so easily.

597
00:36:47,170 --> 00:36:49,970
Search the riverbank carefully
for anyone acting suspiciously.

598
00:36:49,970 --> 00:36:50,450
Got it.

599
00:36:54,090 --> 00:36:54,690
Thank you.

600
00:37:00,170 --> 00:37:01,230
I'll take them all.

601
00:37:16,820 --> 00:37:17,480
Eunuch Zhu.

602
00:37:17,530 --> 00:37:19,060
No sign of the Crown Prince.

603
00:37:23,470 --> 00:37:24,050
Go.

604
00:37:24,860 --> 00:37:26,420
Send word to Xie Sanfa.

605
00:37:27,870 --> 00:37:30,270
Once the four of them
are confirmed aboard,

606
00:37:30,290 --> 00:37:32,950
locking the cabin door
will serve as the signal.

607
00:37:33,310 --> 00:37:34,350
That Zhu fellow

608
00:37:34,980 --> 00:37:36,980
must be somewhere nearby right now.

609
00:37:37,610 --> 00:37:39,340
Don't let him suspect a thing

610
00:37:39,530 --> 00:37:41,610
before he comes aboard.

611
00:37:41,630 --> 00:37:42,360
Understood.

612
00:38:49,430 --> 00:38:50,530
You drank the most last night.

613
00:38:50,530 --> 00:38:51,740
Didn't I warn you?

614
00:38:52,300 --> 00:38:52,970
Xie Sanfa.

615
00:38:54,210 --> 00:38:55,280
Why are you here so late?

616
00:38:55,280 --> 00:38:56,480
Are we leaving or not?

617
00:38:57,170 --> 00:38:58,360
Without a letter of passage,

618
00:38:58,360 --> 00:39:00,330
I'll lose money on this shipment.

619
00:39:04,630 --> 00:39:12,330
♪ Boats lie moored
at Guazhou Ferry Wharf ♪

620
00:39:05,010 --> 00:39:06,670
Due to the limited current of the canal,

621
00:39:06,670 --> 00:39:07,920
navigation is difficult.

622
00:39:07,920 --> 00:39:10,310
This permit is hereby issued
as authorization

623
00:39:10,310 --> 00:39:12,150
for the vessel to depart on schedule.

624
00:39:12,150 --> 00:39:13,190
They really got it!

625
00:39:13,190 --> 00:39:20,890
♪ Tribute ships are laden with
fresh goods ♪

626
00:39:14,740 --> 00:39:15,740
To the boatman...

627
00:39:17,110 --> 00:39:18,090
Xie Sanfa.

628
00:39:19,070 --> 00:39:20,670
Are you getting aboard or not?

629
00:39:20,670 --> 00:39:22,200
If not, we're setting sail.

630
00:39:22,200 --> 00:39:29,600
♪ Brokers and their chiefs
haggle over their deals ♪

631
00:39:22,220 --> 00:39:23,130
We are, we are. Definitely...

632
00:39:23,130 --> 00:39:23,900
Why?

633
00:39:23,990 --> 00:39:25,190
You're setting sail?

634
00:39:25,400 --> 00:39:27,530
That letter of passage is meant for me.

635
00:39:27,700 --> 00:39:29,500
How are you planning to set sail?

636
00:39:29,740 --> 00:39:31,700
Three-legged toads are hard to come by,

637
00:39:30,840 --> 00:39:41,890
♪ The entire world bustles,
chasing profit ♪

638
00:39:31,900 --> 00:39:33,340
but two-legged boatmen

639
00:39:33,920 --> 00:39:35,850
are a dime a dozen around this dock.

640
00:39:36,030 --> 00:39:36,700
Sanfa.

641
00:39:37,510 --> 00:39:38,570
He's just teasing you.

642
00:39:38,570 --> 00:39:39,500
Come up quickly.

643
00:39:41,220 --> 00:39:41,940
Hurry up.

644
00:39:49,070 --> 00:39:49,870
Is it genuine?

645
00:39:53,150 --> 00:39:56,480
It says "Xie Sanfa." It bears
the official government seal.

646
00:39:57,260 --> 00:39:57,740
Sanfa.

647
00:39:57,820 --> 00:39:58,280
So next,

648
00:39:58,280 --> 00:39:59,280
are we going to...

649
00:39:59,320 --> 00:39:59,980
Get to work.

650
00:40:23,610 --> 00:40:24,540
We should be able

651
00:40:25,420 --> 00:40:27,350
to reach Beijing in 10 days, right?

652
00:40:27,900 --> 00:40:30,430
We'll travel day and night
without stopping.

653
00:40:30,820 --> 00:40:32,100
With this letter of passage,

654
00:40:32,100 --> 00:40:34,360
we'll get priority at the dams and locks.

655
00:40:35,180 --> 00:40:36,440
No need to wait in line.

656
00:40:37,340 --> 00:40:38,610
If we're lucky

657
00:40:38,860 --> 00:40:40,390
and catch a favorable wind,

658
00:40:40,570 --> 00:40:41,900
we can cover 200 to 300 li

659
00:40:42,050 --> 00:40:43,740
in a single day and night.

660
00:40:44,450 --> 00:40:45,420
At this rate,

661
00:40:45,630 --> 00:40:47,890
we'll definitely make it within 10 days.

662
00:40:49,450 --> 00:40:51,130
Didn't you say 4 cormorants were boarding?

663
00:40:51,130 --> 00:40:52,130
Is everyone here?

664
00:40:53,920 --> 00:40:55,250
Here comes another one.

665
00:40:57,720 --> 00:40:59,380
Aren't you still missing one?

666
00:41:00,110 --> 00:41:01,940
What, are you going to

667
00:41:02,550 --> 00:41:04,350
refund my money for missing one?

668
00:41:05,150 --> 00:41:07,300
We agreed on the terms beforehand.

669
00:41:07,490 --> 00:41:09,030
Did you take the money or not?

670
00:41:09,030 --> 00:41:09,610
I did.

671
00:41:10,360 --> 00:41:11,760
Since you took the money,

672
00:41:11,940 --> 00:41:13,600
you set sail when I tell you to.

673
00:41:13,780 --> 00:41:15,490
No more arguing or making excuses.

674
00:41:15,490 --> 00:41:16,220
Understood?

675
00:41:28,820 --> 00:41:30,450
You've been running back and forth.

676
00:41:30,450 --> 00:41:31,450
What are you up to?

677
00:41:32,340 --> 00:41:34,340
I'm just securing the spare anchor.

678
00:41:35,830 --> 00:41:37,960
Do you think I'm an idiot or something?

679
00:41:39,510 --> 00:41:41,110
I'm warning all three of you.

680
00:41:41,800 --> 00:41:43,260
Don't try anything funny.

681
00:41:49,030 --> 00:41:49,570
How is it?

682
00:41:50,720 --> 00:41:51,520
I've checked.

683
00:41:51,970 --> 00:41:53,610
Didn't see anyone suspicious.

684
00:41:53,610 --> 00:41:54,420
That's good.

685
00:41:55,340 --> 00:41:56,640
Young Master was right.

686
00:41:56,640 --> 00:41:57,970
Better safe than sorry.

687
00:42:12,100 --> 00:42:13,160
When do we set sail?

688
00:42:13,170 --> 00:42:14,630
We'll be leaving shortly.

689
00:42:16,130 --> 00:42:16,700
Sanfa.

690
00:42:17,640 --> 00:42:19,570
There are 4 cormorants in there.
None missing.

691
00:42:19,570 --> 00:42:21,430
There's another one in the cabin.

692
00:42:22,860 --> 00:42:23,530
Sanfa.

693
00:42:24,770 --> 00:42:26,140
These four are definitely
no ordinary bunch.

694
00:42:26,140 --> 00:42:27,260
Last night, even Wang Ji

695
00:42:27,260 --> 00:42:28,750
and that eunuch were afraid of them.

696
00:42:28,750 --> 00:42:30,150
Maybe we should just run.

697
00:42:30,350 --> 00:42:31,330
Shut up, okay?

698
00:42:31,670 --> 00:42:32,870
Let's go. Come on.

699
00:42:36,740 --> 00:42:37,440
There's no time

700
00:42:37,440 --> 00:42:38,770
to think about that now.

701
00:42:38,800 --> 00:42:40,260
Get the spare anchor chain.

702
00:42:40,260 --> 00:42:40,820
What for?

703
00:42:42,130 --> 00:42:44,060
We'll lock them in the cabin first.

704
00:42:44,780 --> 00:42:46,380
We're dead either way,

705
00:42:47,930 --> 00:42:49,490
so we might as well put up a fight.
